Chapter: TupleSlice2
  cites Foreword chapter Tuple
  cites Codex chapter General

 The `(A, B)` type shorthand in signatures and `let (x, y) = e`
 destructuring — sugar over `Tup2 A B` and a single-arm match.

Section: Definitions

  swap-pair : (Integer, Integer) -> (Integer, Integer)
  swap-pair (p) =
    let (a, b) = p
    in (b, a)

  add-pair : (Integer, Integer) -> Integer
  add-pair (p) =
    let (x, y) = p
    in x + y

  sum-triple : (Integer, Integer, Integer) -> Integer
  sum-triple (t) =
    let (a, b, c) = t
    in a + b + c

  compute : Integer
  compute =
    let q = swap-pair (10, 20)
    in let s = add-pair q
    in s + sum-triple (1, 2, 6)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show compute)
  end

